direction: right

# ============================================================================
# CHANGELOG - Mobile Commerce Architecture
# ============================================================================
#
# All notable changes to this architecture diagram are documented here.
# Format based on Keep a Changelog (https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/)
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [2026-01-03] - TO-BE Architecture Updates
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ADDED:
# ------
# • New CRM Platform Integration
#   - Component: New CRM Platform (Customer Master)
#   - Integration Type: Account data replication
#   - Trigger: Customer account creation event
#   - Direction: Backend (.NET App Services) → New CRM Platform
#
#   Payload Schema:
#   {
#     "emailAddress": "string (required)",
#     "contactPreferences": {
#       "marketing": "boolean",
#       "sms": "boolean",
#       "email": "boolean",
#       "push": "boolean"
#     }
#   }
#
#   Technical Details:
#   - Protocol: REST JSON API
#   - Authentication: OAuth 2.0
#   - Purpose: Creates customer master record in CRM
#   - Impacted Regions: All (East US, West Europe, Southeast Asia)
#
#   Business Justification:
#   - Centralizes customer data in CRM platform
#   - Enables marketing automation and customer segmentation
#   - Supports GDPR compliance through centralized contact preferences
#   - Provides single source of truth for customer contact information
#
# CHANGED:
# --------
# • Migration Details Summary - Updated to include three major changes:
#   1. eCommerce Platform Migration (existing)
#      - Product READ: XML → REST JSON
#      - Account SYNC: SOAP → REST + OAuth 2.0
#
#   2. Loyalty Platform Migration (existing)
#      - Response schema: +6 new attributes
#      - Enhanced reward tracking & history
#
#   3. New CRM Platform Integration (NEW)
#      - CREATE: Account replication to CRM
#      - Payload: emailAddress, contactPreferences
#
# VISUAL UPDATES:
# ---------------
# • Added newCRM component (cylinder shape, teal #e1f5fe)
# • Added connections from all Azure App Services to CRM
# • Connection styled in teal (#00897b) for new integration
# • Added 🆕 emoji indicator for new integrations
# • Updated legend with "New Integration" category
#
# SCENARIO BEHAVIOR:
# ------------------
# • AS-IS: CRM component hidden (opacity: 0)
# • TO-BE: CRM component visible with full opacity
# • Legacy systems shown with reduced opacity (0.2) in TO-BE
#
# IMPLEMENTATION NOTES:
# ---------------------
# Backend Changes Required:
# - Implement CRM client service for API communication
# - Add OAuth 2.0 authentication flow for CRM platform
# - Create account creation event handler
# - Map customer data to CRM payload schema
# - Implement retry logic and error handling
# - Add monitoring and alerting for CRM integration
#
# Testing Considerations:
# - Unit tests for payload mapping and validation
# - Integration tests with CRM sandbox environment
# - End-to-end tests for account creation flow
# - Load testing for concurrent account creations
# - Failure scenario testing (CRM unavailable, timeout)
#
# Deployment Strategy:
# - Feature flag controlled rollout
# - Gradual rollout by region (East US → West Europe → Southeast Asia)
# - Monitor CRM API latency and error rates
# - Rollback plan if CRM causes account creation delays
#
# MIGRATION RISKS:
# ----------------
# - Data consistency: Account creation in eCommerce + CRM must be atomic
# - Performance: CRM API calls may slow down account creation
# - Dependency: New external dependency on CRM platform availability
# - Data privacy: GDPR compliance for customer data replication
# - Schema evolution: CRM schema changes require backend updates
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Initial] - AS-IS Architecture
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - Legacy eCommerce platform integration (XML/SOAP)
# - Legacy Loyalty platform integration
# - Multi-region Azure deployment (East US, West Europe, Southeast Asia)
# - Cloudflare WAF protection
# - iOS and Android mobile applications
#
# ============================================================================

classes: {
  hidden: {
    style.opacity: 0
  }
  legacy: {
    style.opacity: .2
  }
}
# Scenario switcher link
